@1 = ~Archer Revised - Combined Archer Overhaul~
@2 = ~Archer Revised - Patch mod-added bows and crossbows for Manyshot (install after item/content mods)~
@100 = ~Archer Revised requires Baldur's Gate: Enhanced Edition, Baldur's Gate II: Enhanced Edition, Enhanced Edition Trilogy (EET), or Icewind Dale: Enhanced Edition.~
@101 = ~Archer Revised replaces the same Archer resources as A7 Improved Archer. Uninstall the Improved Archer component before installing Archer Revised.~
@102 = ~Archer Revised replaces the same Archer kit as Artisan's Kitpack: Archer Overhaul. Uninstall component 2010 before installing Archer Revised.~

@103 = ~The late-install Manyshot item patch requires the Archer Revised core component.~
@104 = ~Artisan's Kitpack Manyshot item tweak (component 20101) is specific to Artisan's Archer implementation and is not compatible with Archer Revised. Use Archer Revised component 10 instead.~
@105 = ~Archer Revised could not locate the Archer proficiency column in WEAPPROF.2DA. Installation has been aborted rather than risk modifying another kit.~
@106 = ~Archer Revised could not identify the vanilla Archer kit and its ability table in KITLIST.2DA.~
@107 = ~No usable Archer/Ranger HLA table was found. The kit will be installed without changing HLA progression. Archer Revised does not enable HLAs in Icewind Dale: Enhanced Edition by itself.~
@108 = ~The current HLA table does not offer Critical Strike. Sure Shot will not be added because its prerequisite would be unavailable.~

@3 = ~Archer Revised - Finalize HLA compatibility (after Skills and Abilities / HLA tweaks)~
@109 = ~The final HLA compatibility patch requires the Archer Revised core component.~
@110 = ~The installed Skills and Abilities HLA catalog has an unsupported format. The compatibility patch was rolled back; no catalog changes were kept.~
@111 = ~Updated the Archer HLA binding and policies in the installed Skills and Abilities catalog.~
